    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is primed for a high-upside Monday, anchored by the strongest trio of the day: **Kyle Tucker** (75.81), **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Kyle Tucker** earns the top spot against Lorenzen, benefiting from a high base projection and a favorable SP xERA of 4.71. **Jackson Merrill** presents an elite play as well; while facing a tougher arm in Gallen, his ability to capitalize on a slow delivery for stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical priority for our squad\u2014combined with an 8th-order slot advantage pushes him over the threshold. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds a premium matchup against Imai, where a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and the second spot in the order solidify his status as a must-start staple for today\u2019s 5x5 rotation.\n\nStrategic depth remains key, and we have opted to prioritize the high-floor production of **Andy Pages** (71.35) and **Cole Carrigg** (61.94) over bench candidates. **Miguel Vargas** provided the most difficult decision, finishing just outside the starting lineup with a 54.41 score. Despite his elite xwOBA of 0.406, the matchup against Tolle provided less efficiency than the platoon-advantaged **Curtis Mead** (60.76), whose dynamic platoon edge against Imai secured his spot in the UTIL slot. We are monitoring **Josh Lowe** closely; while his 49.19 score justifies a start, the presence of deGrom on the mound remains a significant risk factor that suppressed his ceiling despite favorable platoon splits. Finally, while we are leaning into speed-heavy profiles like **Nasim Nunez** (60.95), we must remain vigilant regarding the low-scoring outings from **Liam Hicks** (47.68) and **Drake Baldwin** (43.62), who are currently battling elite arms and unfavorable park conditions.",
